# Fathom — Screens, menus, and the HUD

This file defines the screens the game shows, how a player moves between them,
the menus each one carries, and the HUD shown while a maze is on screen. The
controls every screen reads are in `specs/movement.md`, and the score, the lives
and the depth the HUD reports are defined in `specs/progression.md`.

## Presentation

Every screen is drawn in the monospace type `specs/overview.md` fixes. Every
piece of text a screen shows is legible against whatever sits behind it at the
logical stage size `1280 x 720`. Where an element sits inside the region this
file gives it, and how it is styled, are yours.

## The screens

`screen` names the screen the game is showing. Every build carries all seven,
and the game opens on `"title"`.

| `screen` | What it shows |
| --- | --- |
| `"title"` | The title `FATHOM`, the tagline `HUNT IN THE DARK`, and the title menu. A dim, dark slice of maze may show behind them. |
| `"howto"` | How to play. |
| `"countdown"` | The maze view and the HUD, with a short `DIVE` countdown drawn over them. |
| `"playing"` | Live play: the dark maze, the forager and its light, the plankton, the bonus drifters, the predators where they are revealed, the sonar wavefronts and ink clouds in flight, and the HUD. |
| `"paused"` | The pause menu, over a maze that stays visible and frozen behind it. |
| `"cleared"` | The interstitial after a maze is cleared, over the maze view, naming the depth just cleared as `DEPTH 1 CLEARED`, `DEPTH 2 CLEARED` and so on. |
| `"gameover"` | The score the run finished on, the depth it reached, and the game-over menu. |

The `"howto"` screen is written in a player's words rather than as rules of a
system, and it covers the controls, naming the key bound to each, the three
predators and the sense each one hunts by, and how a dark maze is read, through
the forager's own light and through the sonar pulse.

## Moving between the screens

| From | On | To |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `"title"` | `DIVE` confirmed | `"countdown"`, at the start of a fresh dive |
| `"title"` | `HOW TO PLAY` confirmed | `"howto"` |
| `"title"` | `back` | `"title"`. Nothing changes. |
| `"howto"` | `confirm` or `back` | `"title"` |
| `"countdown"` | The countdown running out | `"playing"` |
| `"playing"` | The pause control | `"paused"` |
| `"playing"` | The forager eating the maze's last plankton | `"cleared"` |
| `"playing"` | Contact with a predator while `lives` is above `0` | `"countdown"`, for another attempt at the same maze and the same depth |
| `"playing"` | Contact with a predator while `lives` is `0` | `"gameover"` |
| `"paused"` | The pause control | `"playing"` |
| `"paused"` | `RESUME` confirmed, or `back` | `"playing"` |
| `"paused"` | `RESTART` confirmed | `"countdown"`, at the start of a fresh dive |
| `"paused"` | `QUIT TO MENU` confirmed | `"title"` |
| `"cleared"` | The interstitial running out | `"countdown"`, at the next depth |
| `"gameover"` | `PLAY AGAIN` confirmed | `"countdown"`, at the start of a fresh dive |
| `"gameover"` | `MENU` confirmed, or `back` | `"title"` |

The dive countdown holds for one fixed length, at least `1 s` and at most `3 s`,
before play begins, and every countdown holds for that same length. The cleared
interstitial holds for at least `1 s` and at most `3 s` before the descent. Both
are timed on the simulation's own accumulated time rather than on the wall
clock, so each gives way after that much game time however the frames that
carried it were drawn.

`Escape` raises `back` and `pause` together on one frame, so `"paused"` reads
`pause` and `back` before the menu's own edges, and a frame carrying either
resumes once and does nothing else. A single `Escape` press on `"playing"`
therefore opens the pause menu and leaves it open, and a single `Escape` press
on `"paused"` resumes play.

## The menus

Each menu is a vertical list of its items, in the order given, stacked one above
the next. One item is selected at a time and the selected item is drawn
distinctly from the others, so a player always sees which item `confirm`
would take. `menuIndex` is that item's index, as `specs/state.md` reports it.
Arriving at the pause menu or at the game-over menu selects that menu's first
item, and arriving at `"title"` selects the entry `titleIndex` holds, which
Returning to the title below fixes. The `up` and `down` controls move the
selection by one item and wrap at both ends, and `confirm` takes the selected
item.

| Menu | Items, in order |
| --- | --- |
| The title menu | `DIVE`, `HOW TO PLAY` |
| The pause menu | `RESUME`, `RESTART`, `QUIT TO MENU` |
| The game-over menu | `PLAY AGAIN`, `MENU` |

What each item does is in the transition table above. The menus take the
controls `specs/movement.md` defines, and the `mute` control is read on every
screen.

### Pointer and touch

Each menu item occupies a rectangular hit region the build lays out.
`specs/instrumentation.md` states the reading through which the build reports an
item's region in logical units, so the menus keep the layout the build chose.

| Input | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| A pointer moves onto an item's region | That item becomes the selected one. |
| A pointer is pressed and released inside one item's region | That item becomes the selected one, and it is confirmed. |
| A touch contact lands inside an item's region | That item becomes the selected one. |
| A touch contact lands and lifts inside one item's region | That item becomes the selected one, and it is confirmed. |

A confirm takes both of its edges inside one item's region: the press and its
release for a pointer, the landing and the lift for a touch contact. Two edges
that fall in different regions, and an edge that falls outside every region,
confirm no item. The item a confirm acts on is the selected one, whichever input
raised it, and what confirming it does is what the transition table above gives
that item.

The how-to-play screen shows no menu, so it carries no item regions. A pointer
pressed and released anywhere on `"howto"`, or a touch contact landing and
lifting anywhere on it, returns to `"title"`, exactly as `confirm` and `back` do,
so the screen is left by hand as well as by key.

## Beginning a dive

`DIVE`, `RESTART` and `PLAY AGAIN` all begin a dive the same way. The score
returns to `0`, the lives to `START_LIVES` (`3`), and the depth to `1`. The maze
is laid out afresh with a plankton on every corridor tile outside the den and
its fog fully unrevealed, every predator is in the den and unreleased, both
cooldowns are ready, and the screen becomes `"countdown"`.

## Returning to the title

Leaving the how-to-play screen, `QUIT TO MENU` on the pause menu, and `MENU` or
`back` on the game-over screen all return to `"title"`.

Confirming an item on the title menu records that item's index as `titleIndex`,
from the keyboard, from a pointer and from a touch contact alike. `titleIndex`
is `0` until an item has been confirmed there, so the game opens with `DIVE`
selected. Every arrival at `"title"` selects the recorded entry: `menuIndex`
becomes `titleIndex`, so each of the three returns above lands on the entry the
player left the title from rather than on the first item.

Returning to `"title"` restores the score, the lives, the depth and the maze to
the values a dive begins from. `titleIndex` is the exception and keeps its value
across the return.

## What advances on each screen

| Screen | What advances |
| --- | --- |
| `"title"`, `"howto"`, `"gameover"` | Nothing. |
| `"countdown"` | The countdown's own remaining time, and the light the forager casts on the maze around it. The forager, the predators, the drifters, the cooldowns, the sonar wavefronts and the ink clouds all hold still. |
| `"playing"` | Everything. |
| `"paused"` | Nothing. The maze behind the menu is frozen. |
| `"cleared"` | The interstitial's own remaining time. |

`simTime` accumulates on every screen, and the controls are read on every
screen.

## The HUD

The HUD is drawn whenever a maze is on screen, which is `"countdown"`, `"playing"`,
`"paused"` and `"cleared"`. It occupies the strips above and below the maze region,
`y` in `[0, 80]` and `y` in `[656, 720]`, so it leaves the maze itself clear. It
is always fully lit, standing outside the fog of war entirely.

Six things are present and readable on it.

| Element | What it reports | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Score | The running score for the whole run, in large digits about `48` logical units tall. | The top strip. |
| Dive label | A small, dim label reading `{{#if (eq variant.slug "kindle")}}KINDLE{{else}}STANDARD{{/if}}`. | The top strip. |
| Lives | The lives remaining, as that many small forager icons. | The bottom strip. |
| Depth | The current depth, as `DEPTH 1`, `DEPTH 2` and so on. | The bottom strip. |
| Sonar gauge | Whether the sonar pulse is ready, as a gauge that is full while it is ready and fills back up as its cooldown runs down. | The bottom strip. |
| Ink gauge | Whether ink is ready, as a gauge that is full while it is ready and fills back up as its cooldown runs down. | The bottom strip. |

Where each of the six sits inside its strip is yours.
